### Cloud Functions Skeleton (`cloud_functions/`)

#### [NEW] `cloud_functions/` directory at project root

Using **Node.js (TypeScript)** for Cloud Functions:

```
cloud_functions/
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
├── src/
│   ├── index.ts                       # Export all functions
│   ├── creditScore.ts                 # Credit score algorithm
│   ├── weatherCheck.ts                # Weather API → disaster detection
│   ├── bnplCalculation.ts             # BNPL interest + penalty math
│   ├── loanEvaluation.ts              # Loan approve/reject based on score
│   └── insurancePayout.ts             # Insurance payout calculation
```

#### [NEW] [creditScore.ts](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/Project/BorneoHack/mobile-games/cloud_functions/src/creditScore.ts)

Algorithm skeleton:

```typescript
// Factors (all from Bank digital payment records, NOT BNPL):
// 1. Payment frequency (how often they use digital payments)
// 2. Payment consistency (regularity over time)
// 3. Average transaction amount
// 4. On-time bill payments vs late
// Score range: 300-850 (mimics real credit scoring)
```

#### [NEW] [weatherCheck.ts](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/Project/BorneoHack/mobile-games/cloud_functions/src/weatherCheck.ts)

```typescript
// 1. Receive user's GPS coords
// 2. Call OpenWeather API
// 3. Check for severe weather alerts (flood, drought, storm)
// 4. If severe → write disaster event to Firestore
// 5. Return disaster status to client
```

---

### Firestore Schema Design

```
users/
  {userId}/
    profile:
      displayName: string
      country: "MY" | "ID" | "SG" | "TH" | "PH" | "VN"
      currency: "XMYR" | "XIDR" | "XSGD" | "XTHB" | "XPHP" | "XVND"
      gpsLat: number
      gpsLng: number
      tutorialCompleted: boolean
      createdAt: timestamp

    wallet:
      cashBalance: number          # Physical cash
      bankBalance: number          # Bank digital account
      bankRegistered: boolean      # Has registered for bank
      totalNetWorth: number        # Computed: cash + bank + farmValue - debt

    creditScore:
      score: number                # 300-850
      lastUpdated: timestamp

    farm:
      plots:                       # Array or sub-collection
        - plotId: string
          tiles: [                 # 2D grid of tile states
            { col, row, crop: "wheat"|"rice"|null, stage: 0-3, plantedAt, insured: bool }
          ]

    financials:
      bnplPlans/
        {planId}:
          itemName: string
          totalAmount: number
          installments: number
          paidInstallments: number
          monthlyAmount: number
          nextDueDate: timestamp
          lateFees: number
          status: "active" | "paid" | "defaulted"

      loans/
        {loanId}:
          principal: number
          interestRate: number
          monthlyPayment: number
          remainingBalance: number
          status: "active" | "paid" | "defaulted"

      insurance/
        {policyId}:
          plotId: string
          premium: number
          coverageAmount: number
          expiresAt: timestamp
          status: "active" | "expired" | "claimed"

      transactions/
        {txId}:
          type: "cash" | "bank"
          category: "crop_sale" | "equipment" | "bnpl_payment" | "loan_payment" | "insurance_premium"
          amount: number
          timestamp: timestamp

    disasterEvents/
      {eventId}:
        type: "flood" | "drought" | "storm"
        severity: number
        cropsDestroyed: number
        insurancePayout: number
        timestamp: timestamp

leaderboards/
  {country}/
    rankings/
      {userId}:
        displayName: string
        netWorth: number
        updatedAt: timestamp
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The `creditScore.score` field is **never** computed on the client. It is only written by the `creditScore` Cloud Function after analyzing the user's `transactions` sub-collection filtered to `type: "bank"` entries only.

